  "body": "> 2. If event’s type attribute value is a match for any of the strings in the first column in the following table, set event’s type attribute value to the string in the second column on the same row as the matching string, and return otherwise.\r\n>\r\n>Event type | Legacy event type\r\n>-- | --\r\n>\"animationend\" | \"webkitAnimationEnd\"\r\n>\"animationiteration\" | \"webkitAnimationIteration\"\r\n>\"animationstart\" | \"webkitAnimationStart\"\r\n>\"transitionend\" | \"webkitTransitionEnd\"\r\n\r\nI saw [this table](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-listener-invoke) not once, but I really can't understand why is there only 4 names of event handlers?\r\n\r\nWhy don't we see for example `\"transitionstart\"` or `\"transitioncancel\"` and so on?\r\n\r\nNeed clarification about this movement in direction these names.\r\n",
